Total internal reflection, evanescent fields and tunnelling (@em-evanescent: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-2-Ellingson.lingua#r_5P52CZD00XV6MMPFY9RHADT5KJ", #source "../sources/Electromagnetic-Waves-and-Antennas-Orfanidis.lingua#r_2E9PTW5TH97W2B200A5XKHHNTQ", #electromagnetism "../matter/Conductivity-complex-permittivity-and-attenuation.lingua#r_4PB9PGW3EFESYNHEZEG2DBRW74") { r_3YG5N7Q50Y4JJ9J7AAHZYRJBCD
**Read:** [Electromagnetics Volume 2 — Steven W. Ellingson](../sources/Electromagnetics-Volume-2-Ellingson.lingua#r_5P52CZD00XV6MMPFY9RHADT5KJ), total internal reflection and evanescent fields; [Electromagnetic Waves and Antennas — Sophocles J. Orfanidis](../sources/Electromagnetic-Waves-and-Antennas-Orfanidis.lingua#r_2E9PTW5TH97W2B200A5XKHHNTQ), evanescent waves and layered structures.

At an interface from higher to lower refractive index, sufficiently large incidence angle makes the transmitted normal wave-vector component imaginary in the ideal lossless model. The transmitted field decays away from the boundary rather than vanishing at it. Reflection has unit power magnitude for an isolated semi-infinite second medium, while its phase depends on angle and polarization.

Derive the critical angle and decay length, and calculate the Poynting vector rather than declaring every evanescent field to carry no energy in every direction. A nearby second interface can couple the decaying field and enable frustrated total internal reflection. The whole arrangement then requires a new boundary problem; a single-interface R = 1 statement no longer determines transmission.

Compare evanescent spatial harmonics in a static boundary solution with those in a harmonic waveguide or interface. Their similar exponential shape does not erase their different time and source conditions. Analyze a finite gap, recover the large-gap limit and identify what changes with loss. Near-field probes can disturb the field they attempt to measure, so the inferred decay length needs an apparatus model and a reference plane.

